🗓️ WEEK 5 — ONLINE PAYMENTS WITH RAZORPAY

Date: Monday, 7 September 2026

🎯 Objective

The objective of Week 5 was to add online payment through Razorpay (UPI and cards) and make sure that only genuine payments create a bill.

🛠️ Work Completed
Created a Razorpay test account and test keys.
Added the Razorpay Node SDK to the backend.
Built the order flow:
The server prices the bag
The server creates a Razorpay order for that amount
The app opens Razorpay Checkout
The customer pays by UPI or card
Built the verify endpoint POST /razorpay/verify.
Saved the bill and reduced stock only after a successful verification.
Showed the digital GST receipt after payment.

⚠️ Error / Problem Faced

After paying, the browser simply tells our app "success", and that message can be faked by anyone.

Until our Razorpay test keys were ready, we could not test payments at all.

A double tap on Pay sent the verify request twice and could create two bills.

✅ Resolution
Verified every payment on the server using the signature returned by Razorpay.
The server recomputes HMAC-SHA256(order_id | payment_id) with the secret key and compares it in constant time.
The bill is saved only if the signatures match; otherwise no invoice is issued.
Wrote a mock gateway for local testing that signs payments with a temporary secret, so the same verification code still runs.
Made verify idempotent: a repeated request returns the same receipt, and an unchanged bag reuses its open order.

🖼️ Project Picture

Checkout screen with UPI, card and cash options, and the Razorpay test-mode payment window.

💡 Learning

We learned that the browser must never be trusted with money.

We also learned how HMAC signatures prove that a message came from someone who holds the secret key.

🔗 UML SEQUENCE DIAGRAM — ONLINE PAYMENT
sequenceDiagram
    actor Customer
    participant Frontend as Frontend (React)
    participant Backend as Backend (Express)
    participant DB as SQLite
    participant Razorpay

    Customer->>Frontend: Tap Pay (UPI / Card)
    Frontend->>Backend: POST /razorpay/orders
    Backend->>DB: read products
    Backend->>Backend: buildBill() GST and round-off
    Backend->>Razorpay: orders.create(amount)
    Razorpay-->>Backend: order_id
    Backend-->>Frontend: orderId, amount, keyId
    Frontend->>Razorpay: open Checkout(order_id)
    Customer->>Razorpay: approve UPI / enter card
    Razorpay-->>Frontend: payment_id + signature
    Frontend->>Backend: POST /razorpay/verify
    Backend->>Backend: verify HMAC-SHA256
    alt signature valid
        Backend->>DB: save bill, stock - qty
        Backend-->>Frontend: receipt (GST invoice)
        Frontend-->>Customer: show receipt
    else invalid
        Backend-->>Frontend: 400 no invoice issued
    end
